   "head_commit": {
    "id": "72f7b9e82c704a586cc75a434378b514f6d0fbce",
    "tree_id": "9c23d01ff6acc01823082c5b2d976dcb2c42c92b",
    "message": "Sizing run: 2,048-bit latch configuration bank through the TT flow\n\nV2_DESIGN 9 first measurement for the latch-configuration risk: take one\nreal block of resettable latches (sg13cmos5l_dlhrq_1) and clock gates\n(sg13cmos5l_lgcp_1, dont_use in the liberty, instantiated) through the\nofficial Tiny Tapeout flow: lint, CTS, STA, precheck and gate-level test.\n\nNot the Metronome design. src/ holds only the sizing top (256-byte bank\nwritten through a pin byte interface, XOR fold and readback mux so no bit\nis optimised away). Config is the passing smoke config of a235fd6 plus\nVERILOG_DEFINES USE_IHP_CELLS. Source of truth for the RTL is\nsim/numerics/v2_sizing/ on metronome-v2.0.\n\nLocal: cocotb RTL smoke 1/1 (Icarus, behavioural cells).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
